---
<ResearchToolArticleLayout title="BMW Scanner Capability Database" description="Compare BMW diagnostic scanners by exact hardware, documented functions, vehicle modules and evidence quality." section="Scanners" sectionHref="/scanners/" readingTime="16 min read" toc={[{"id":"scanner-shortlist","label":"Scanner shortlist"},{"id":"functions","label":"Function verification"},{"id":"source-led-research","label":"Research and limitations"},{"id":"primary-sources","label":"Sources"},{"id":"related-guides","label":"Related articles"}]}>
<div class="capability-shell"><div class="tool-research-intro">
<p class="lede">The useful question is not which scan-tool brand is best. It is <strong>which exact hardware SKU and software entitlement can perform your required operation on the specific BMW chassis, model year, and control module</strong> — with adequate safety and documented update rights.</p>
<p>Generic “all-systems” language rarely tells a BMW owner whether a device supports a specific ABS fault, parking brake service routine, battery registration, coding procedure, or official guided test plan. We separate vendor-described product capabilities from verified vehicle-specific eligibility. This tool has not been independently tested on actual vehicles. Read the source and its limitations before assuming support.</p>
</div>

<figure><picture><source media="(max-width:650px)" srcset="/images/tools/bmw-scanner-capability-database/capability-layers-mobile.svg"/><img src="/images/tools/bmw-scanner-capability-database/capability-layers.svg" width="1200" height="450" loading="lazy" alt="BMW scanner selection through chassis, control module, operation, tool SKU, software license and safe procedure"/></picture><figcaption>A brand-level scan-tool feature list is only one part of the compatibility decision.</figcaption></figure>
<section class="panel">
<h2 id="scanner-shortlist">Filter the documented scanner shortlist</h2><p>Five <strong>product families or exact models</strong> are presented with candid evidence limits; this is a research directory, not a laboratory ranking. The Launch family row is not an exact device specification and is excluded when you filter for exact model records.</p>
<div class="filters"><label>Manufacturer <select id="manufacturer"><option value="all">All manufacturers</option><option value="Foxwell">Foxwell</option><option value="Autel">Autel</option><option value="Launch">Launch</option></select></label><label>Evidence row type <select id="rowtype"><option value="all">All rows</option><option value="exact">Exact model identified</option><option value="family">Family; exact model still needed</option></select></label></div>
<p id="result-count" role="status" aria-live="polite">Showing five researched rows.</p>
<div class="scroll"><table><caption>Vendor-claimed general capabilities; vehicle-specific functions require confirmation</caption><thead><tr><th>Scanner</th><th>Product category</th><th>Documented boundary</th><th>What cannot be inferred</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{models.map(m=><tr data-maker={m.maker} data-kind={m.name==='Launch X-431'?'family':'exact'}><th scope="row">{m.name}</th><td>{m.category}</td><td>{m.coverage}</td><td>{m.caveat}</td><td><a href={m.link} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Manufacturer ↗</a></td></tr>)}
</tbody></table></div><p id="empty" hidden>No rows in this limited source set fit the selection. This does not establish that no suitable diagnostic device exists.</p>
</section>
<section><h2 id="functions">Functions that must be checked individually</h2><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Required BMW task</th><th>Documentable general category</th><th>Vehicle-level verification still required</th><th>Related research</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Full-vehicle fault survey</td><td>OEM-level or full-system diagnostics where listed</td><td>Accessible ECU list, supported chassis, age and installed systems</td><td><a href="/tools/bmw-scanner-capability-database/#bmw-code-reader-vs-scan-tool">Reader versus scanner</a></td></tr>
<tr><td>ABS / airbag diagnosis</td><td>Module read/erase and live data</td><td>Exact brake or restraint ECU coverage and fault context</td><td><a href="/guides/bmw-scanner-abs-airbag-codes/">ABS / airbag scanners</a></td></tr>
<tr><td>Battery registration</td><td>Battery management service function</td><td>Battery type, model year, registration versus coding distinction</td><td><a href="/guides/bmw-battery-registration-scanner/">Battery registration</a></td></tr>
<tr><td>Active component testing</td><td>Bidirectional active test where manufacturer lists it</td><td>Specific module, command, prerequisite, safety risk</td><td><a href="/guides/bmw-bidirectional-scan-tool-functions/">Active-test guide</a></td></tr>
<tr><td>EPB service mode or brake bleed</td><td>Service and actuator functions on supported vehicles</td><td>OEM brake service procedure and tool coverage</td><td><a href="/guides/bmw-brake-bleed-scan-tool/">Brake bleed guide</a></td></tr>
<tr><td>DoIP / CAN FD support</td><td>Vendor protocol and VCI transport specification</td><td>Required vehicle-generation network path and interface revision</td><td><a href="/guides/foxwell-nt710-vs-autel-mk900-bmw/">NT710 versus MK900</a></td></tr>
<tr><td>Coding / ECU programming</td><td>Separate operation class; never infer from active-test support</td><td>Exact approved model, official program and recovery environment</td><td><a href="/guides/bmw-coding-vs-programming/">Coding versus programming</a></td></tr>
</tbody></table></div></section>
<figure><picture><source media="(max-width:650px)" srcset="/images/tools/bmw-scanner-capability-database/risk-boundaries-mobile.svg"/><img src="/images/tools/bmw-scanner-capability-database/risk-boundaries.svg" width="1200" height="450" loading="lazy" alt="Read-only scan, active tests, service procedures and programming have increasing operation-specific prerequisites"/></picture><figcaption>A scanner that reads codes cannot automatically perform active tests, adaptations or firmware programming.</figcaption></figure>
<section id="source-led-research"><ScannerResearch/></section>
<ConsolidatedScannerLegacyResearch />
<section class="panel"><h2 id="primary-sources">Primary sources and disclosure of evidence quality</h2><p>Evidence reviewed October 9, 2026. Vendor literature states platform-wide feature categories; the manufacturer or tool's exact vehicle-function lookup determines eligibility. We have not connected these devices to a car, verified a live scan, or performed workshop repairs. No affiliate ranking or live retailer pricing is embedded in this reference.</p><ul>
<li><a href="https://www.autel.com/mk2/3990.jhtml">Autel MK808S/MK808Z official specifications</a></li>
<li><a href="https://autel.com/mk3/4171.jhtml">Autel MK900 official product information and comparison</a></li>
<li><a href="https://www.autel.com/u/cms/www/202604/200157383ity.pdf">Autel MK900 user manual — ECU info, live data, tests and special functions</a></li>
<li><a href="https://www.foxwelltech.us/product-detail-524.html">Foxwell NT530 technical specifications and manuals</a></li><li><a href="https://www.foxwelldiag.com/products/foxwell-nt710">Foxwell NT710 model-specific description, supported BMW coding and service categories</a></li><li><a href="https://www.foxwelldiag.com/pages/buyer-guide">Foxwell model comparison and coverage disclaimer</a></li>
<li><a href="https://www.cnlaunch.com/">Launch manufacturer — verify exact X-431 model and VCI</a></li>
</ul></section>
<section class="panel"><h2 id="related-guides">Related Chassis Signal articles</h2><p>The original pairwise comparisons have been merged into this resource and now 301-redirect here. They offer deeper comparisons, module-specific cautions, documented model exceptions and original diagrams that should not be lost to a generic database.</p><div class="related-grid">{related.map(([slug,title,desc])=><article><h3><a href={consolidatedRedirects[slug] ? `${consolidatedRedirects[slug]}#${slug}` : `/guides/${slug}/`}>{title} →</a></h3><p>{desc}</p></article>)}</div></section>
</div>
<script>
const maker=document.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('#manufacturer')!,kind=document.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('#rowtype')!,rows=[...document.querySelectorAll<HTMLTableRowElement>('tr[data-maker]')],count=document.querySelector('#result-count')!,empty=document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#empty')!;function update(){let n=0;for(const row of rows){const keep=(maker.value==='all'||row.dataset.maker===maker.value)&&(kind.value==='all'||row.dataset.kind===kind.value);row.hidden=!keep;if(keep)n++}count.textContent=`Showing ${n} of ${rows.length} researched models and families.`;empty.hidden=n>0}maker.addEventListener('change',update);kind.addEventListener('change',update);update();
</script>
